  "facts": [
    "Apollo Bridge, opened September 5, 2005, spans 231 metres across the Danube, its curved lines and inclined arches giving it a uniquely sophisticated geometric shape.",
    "During construction, engineers rotated the 5,240‑ton steel structure 231 metres from its left‑bank site to a pillar 40 metres from the right bank, a first in Europe.",
    "Named after the nearby Apollo oil refinery, the bridge earned a 2006 nomination as one of five finalists for the American Society of Civil Engineers’ Outstanding Civil Engineering Achievement Award."
